Description: Library sidebar: order, hide and rename sections; navigation controls
 The sidebar sections (library features) follow [Library] SidebarOrder (keys
 = icon names, comma separated; unlisted ones follow in Mixxx's order),
 [Library] SidebarHidden hides sections and [Library] SidebarLabels
 (key=Label;...) renames them. Preferences > Library > Sidebar edits all
 three: tick to show, double-click to rename, drag or Up/Down to order; the
 order and hidden sections apply at the next start, labels at once.
 Controls for skins and controllers, so that they never count sidebar rows:
 [Library],show_<key> (show_tracks, show_autodj, show_playlist,
 show_crates, show_computer, show_history, ...) selects and opens a section;
 [Library],active_<key> is 1 while that section or one of its lists is
 shown; [Library],sidebar_up selects the parent of the selected sidebar item
 (a folder's parent, a list's section); [Library],sidebar_at_top is 1 while
 a section itself is selected. Mixxx has no way to order or rename the
 sidebar.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
